 jj's book suggests that they can  help to draw  toxins out of the body while you sleep  the reality is  toxin eliminating foot treatments like  ionic foot baths  have been thoroughly debunked by the  medical community  it's literally a pretty common snake oil  scam  the only reason you would see any color  changes that may be used as  evidence of toxins leaving the body is  because of some  natural chemical reactions with various  salts and ions  so to sum it up obviously  this detox is not evidence-based and  potentially  dangerous considering you're supposed to  do this  routine for 10 whole days  so if you want real safe detox methods  just eat some food drink some water go  for a walk  and then proceed to sweat piss crap and  breathe out the toxins  because safe detoxing is what your body  is naturally designed  to do hard stuff  anyways i'm getting riled up on this  detox bs but  that is not what this video is about now  back to the public's reaction  to put it succinctly lizzo's fans  were not impressed they were attacking  her for promoting diet culture  and seemingly contradicting everything  they believed  that she stood for now i have to be  totally honest when these videos came  out  i got about a million and one dms about  them  filled with genuine concern that this  body positive queen  was transitioning to the dark side of  diet culture  and i admit i was really taken aback by  the video series myself  but it was not because i thought lizzo  was letting down the fat community  or denouncing her vow of self-love  as i've said a million times in a  million different videos  i believe in body autonomy and you're  not a failure at loving yourself  if you want to lose weight i'm also not  even going to debate whether or not  lizzo's before and after shots were  proof that she was doing the cleanse for  weight loss rather than for  digestion and health honestly these days  the lines are so blurred between one's  concern  around reducing like bloating versus  reducing fat  and that is all a moot point anyway  i strongly believe that lizzo can do  whatever the hell she wants with her  body  and i will support her because she's  smart  beautiful and a truly talented artist  plus truth hurts will forever go down as  one of my all-time  favorite songs period we just keep it  pushing like  but we shouldn't be upset at lizzo for  wanting to do a detox  or lose weight we should be upset with  diet culture  itself and the system that allows  pseudoscience and nutrition  misinformation  to occupy every communication stream we  access  i believe strongly and i always have  said this  that all public personalities  influencers  and celebrities possess incredible  responsibility  to vet the claims that they make about  the things that they share  publicly even if it's prefaced by this  is just what i'm doing  do your own research we all know that a  lot of  young impressionable fans lack the  critical thinking skills to do  anything but emulate their idols so i  feel at least  that it's fair to be disappointed that  lizza would promote a protocol  with no evidence to back it up that in  fact could be  really devastating in the wrong hands i  am  also annoyed that she partnered with a  nutritionist j.j smith whose  education includes a certificate from  the institute of holistic healing  a course that i could find no legitimate  information about  online and who exclusively promotes  sensationalized protocols  like the seven day apple cider vinegar  cleanse  in addition to the smoothie one that  lizzo did but  lizzo is not a superhuman she is  susceptible to  snake oil salespeople and  sensationalized  wellness promises just like the rest of  us  in fact in a follow-up post lizzo said  that  i spent so much time in this body and i  am no different than you  still struggling to find balance still  trying to mend my relationship with food  with my anxiety my back fat if i have  any advice  it's to eat drink move rest your job is  to 